course: dictionary
lesson: 1294
title: Buzzing: a sound, a crowd, a feeling
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Buzzing is first of all a sound. In «What elephants really fear is the buzzing of angry bees», the buzzing is the low humming noise that bees make when they beat their wings very fast. The words angry bees are your clue: bees are the ones that buzz.
explain: Buzzing can also describe a place full of life. «The hall was buzzing» does not mean the hall hums. Swap in your meaning: full of noise, busy people and excitement fits the sentence, so that is the right meaning.
explain: Buzzing with feeling means very excited. In British and Irish slang, someone who says «I'm buzzing about the trip!» is very happy and excited. The same word can mean a sound, a crowd or a feeling, so always check the words around it to choose the right meaning.
fact: Buzzing means making a low humming sound, like a bee or a fly.
fact: Buzzing can also mean full of activity, noise and excitement, as in «The hall was buzzing».
fact: In British and Irish slang, buzzing means very happy and excited.
fact: To buzz someone in means pressing a button to open a door for them.
fact: A buzzer in a science circuit makes a buzzing noise.
exercise: «What elephants really fear is the buzzing of angry bees, which can sting the soft skin inside the trunk and round the eyes.» What is the buzzing? | A kind of wild flower | A soft, gentle song | *A low humming sound made by bees | A sort of bee-shaped hat
exercise: «The hall was buzzing before the match.» What does buzzing mean here? | *Full of noise, activity and excitement | Very quiet and still | Humming like a bee | Empty and broken
exercise: Jo says, «Press the button to buzz me in.» What does buzz me in mean? | To send me a bee | To hum a song to me | To lock the door behind me | *To open the door for me by pressing a button
test: Tom says, «I'm buzzing about the trip!» What does buzzing mean? | Making a humming noise | Stung by a bee | *Very happy and excited | Waiting quietly
test: Which thing in a science lesson makes a buzzing noise? | A glass of water | A thermometer | A magnet | *A buzzer in a circuit
exam: Find the best meaning of buzzing in «The classroom was buzzing with ideas after the trip.» | *Full of activity, noise and excitement | Asleep and silent | Covered in bee stings | Making the sound of a fly's wings only
